{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.CEqualsBarIffAll1dim","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.CEqualsBarIffAll1dim","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.eigenvalues_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.eigenvalues_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L139-L150","doc":"The two Hecke eigenvalues are genuinely distinct exactly when `q² ≠ -1`.\nUnder the additive toy both collapsed onto the same element for every `q`,\nwhich is precisely why the second case could not be stated there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.cOnEigenvalue_neg_q_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.cOnEigenvalue_neg_q_inv","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L131-L137","doc":"`C = bar` on the eigenvalue `-q⁻¹`: `C(-q⁻¹) = -q⁻¹ - h = -q = bar(-q⁻¹)`.\nThis is the case the additive toy could not state; it is *false* there and\ntrue here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.cOnEigenvalue_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.cOnEigenvalue_q","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L126-L129","doc":"`C = bar` on the eigenvalue `q`: `C(q) = q - h = q⁻¹ = bar(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.cOnEigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.cOnEigenvalue","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L123-L124","doc":"`C` acts on a one-dimensional eigenvalue by `α ↦ α - h`, from `σ⁻¹ = σ - h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.heckeH","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L120-L121","doc":"The Hecke parameter `h = q - q⁻¹`, with `q` a unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.c_equals_bar_on_one_dim_eigenvalue_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.c_equals_bar_on_one_dim_eigenvalue_q","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L65-L73","doc":"C = bar at H₂ (1-dim only).\nOn a 1-dim rep with eigenvalue α:\n  C: α → α⁻¹  (from σ⁻¹ = σ − h, eigenvalue α − h)\n  bar: α → α⁻¹  (from q → q⁻¹, eigenvalue q → q⁻¹)\nThese agree when α ∈ {q, −q⁻¹}:\n  C(q) = q − h = q − (q − q⁻¹) = q⁻¹ = bar(q)  ✓\n  C(−q⁻¹) = −q⁻¹ − h = −q = bar(−q⁻¹)  ✓  ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.oneDimIrreps_exhaust_h2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.oneDimIrreps_exhaust_h2","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L58-L63","doc":"At `H₂` the 1-dim irreps exhaust the algebra: `oneDimIrrepCount` of\nthem, each of dimension 1, square-sum to `dim H₂ = 2!`.  False for any\nother count, so the constant is doing work here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.oneDimIrrepCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.oneDimIrrepCount","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L40-L56","doc":"The number of 1-dim irreps of `S_n` for `n ≥ 2` — the trivial and the\nsign representation.  A **named constant**, not a theorem.\n\nReplaced `theorem exactly_two_one_dim_irreps : (2 : ℕ) = 2 := rfl`\n(2026-08-21; vacuity ledger, `reflexive-tautology-ascribed-literal`).\n`2 = 2` holds however many 1-dim irreps `S_n` has, so it asserted\nnothing; per Strict Lean Discipline §8 a statement with no falsifiable\ncontent is notation and belongs in a `def`.\n\nThe general justification the old docstring gave — that `S_n` has\nexactly two homomorphisms to `ℤ/2ℤ` — is **not** formalised here (it\nneeds `Mathlib`'s symmetric-group representation theory).  What this\nfile *does* prove is the `H₂` case, from the other direction:\n`two_only_unit_squares` shows `1² + 1² = 2` is the unique decomposition\nof `dim H₂ = 2!` into positive squares, so at `H₂` these two exhaust the\nalgebra and no multi-dimensional irrep can exist. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.factorial_exceeds_two_squares","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.factorial_exceeds_two_squares","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L32-L38","doc":"For n ≥ 3: n! ≥ 6 > 2 = 1² + 1², so the two 1-dim irreps\ncannot exhaust the algebra dimension. Multi-dim irreps forced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.h3_has_multidim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.h3_has_multidim","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L29-L30","doc":"At H₃: n! = 6 = 1² + 2² + 1². A 2-dim irrep EXISTS. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.two_only_unit_squares","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.two_only_unit_squares","kind":"theorem","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L21-L27","doc":"2 = 1² + 1² is the UNIQUE decomposition of 2 as a sum of\npositive squares. No multi-dim irrep can exist at H₂. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim","label":"prop:c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.h2_all_one_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.h2_all_one_dim","kind":"theorem","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/c-equals-bar-iff-all-1dim.lean#L18-L19","doc":"At H₂: n! = 2 = 1² + 1². All irreps are 1-dim. ","signatureChunk":0}]}